    "title": "One person killed in early morning crash on SH 288 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chad Washington ,\n16 hours ago\nHOUSTON ( CW39 ) - A fatal crash on an exit ramp on State Highway 288 that was impacting traffic Wednesday morning in south Houston has cleared.\nThe crash happened around 4:45 a.m. Wednesday morning, according to Houston Transtar . The debris landed on an exit ramp just south of Beltway 8, Pearland police said.\nThe driver of the vehicle was declared dead at the scene, police said.\nThe investigation continues but all southbound lanes of the South Freeway were closed beginning north of the Beltway until Clear Creek. They were reopened and the accident was cleared around 9:46 a.m. according to Houston Transtar.\nNorthbound lanes on Highway 288 are fully open, as well as all lanes of the Highway 288 toll road. To help navigate the area, please use the CW39 traffic map .\nHouston news Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CW39 Houston.",
